{"title":"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a regular octagon, the sum of any three consecutive sides is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03fa3795d07527af8700c3fded230607baf1fec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> A square is constructed using one of the sides of this octagon. What is the area of the square?\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Octagonsquare.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bf/Octagonsquare.jpg/250px-Octagonsquare.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"254\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bf/Octagonsquare.jpg/375px-Octagonsquare.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bf/Octagonsquare.jpg/500px-Octagonsquare.jpg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that the sum of any three sides of the octagon is 90, and since the octagon is regular, we know that all sides are equal. Thus, each side of the octagon must equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/63273d935564ff32da9eb73992a1e4f5ca3c7713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{90}{3} = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />. Since one side of the square shares a side with the octagon, we know the side lengths of the square are also 30. Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/e/d7e2dffb331b03f5b54f9935fcab0c97b43108e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^2 = \\boxed{900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"23\" /> \n</p><p>~Bradygho\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have each side of the octagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d7c52564f6e676db31ecc1ad9b611f7f0de9a66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3s=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df29ca19d830366a9e5d6689b79698abe5d4535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=30$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />. This means the area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/7/d97e823c98f0108aedf170fda5cdfea95ac5e7c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^2=\\boxed{900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~Geometry285\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems\">Other 2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017155532\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 50/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1199/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   27.836      1 Template:JMPSC_Notice\n100.00%   27.836      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21581:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017155532 and revision id 158064. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}